iterations.reply:
The `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so importing `http-client` would fail linking again. The planned grant isn't in the graph yet, so I've removed the import and the enrichment fetch. The reply path doesn't depend on the fetch, so the output is the same. I also added guards so the body traps rather than returning a confirmation that violates `ensures`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // ensures delivered == true and present(session_id): the output must
        // satisfy both. If the channel does not confirm delivery or does not
        // return a session identity, trap rather than emit a violating output.
        if !confirmation.delivered {
            panic!("SendReply: channel did not confirm delivery");
        }
        if confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply: channel returned no session identity");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

